<title>CHINA: Shanghai T-bill market closed for holiday.</title>
<headline>Shanghai T-bill market closed for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shanghai's T-bill repo and spot market was closed on Monday because of a National Day holiday, an exchange official said. Trading will resume on Thursday.</p>
<p>On Friday, the last trading day, the annual rate for the most active three-day contract fell to 7.13 percent from 24.40 percent on Thursday.</p>
<p>On the spot market, the most active 10-year bond that matures in June 2006 closed slightly up at 120.91 yuan from 120.90 yuan.</p>
</text>
